description:
The user asked whether clicking a citation could highlight the cited text in the reader. Highlighting already exists: PdfViewer matches citation.excerpt against the pdf.js text layer (text-highlight.ts, evidence.ts) and marks the supporting sentences strong and the rest context. Outcomes are 'highlighted' or 'page-only'. On 2026-10-09 the lead clicked 9 citations across 3 papers in the user's running app, and all 9 reported 'Highlighted the cited passage'. Screenshots show the problems:
- the strong highlight is a faint pale yellow that is easy to miss on dense pages;
- the context marks are invisible;
- the reader scrolls to the cited page rather than centring the passage;
- when text matching fails, the reader only jumps to the page.
Citations already carry block-level bboxes ([page, x0, y0, x1, y1] in PDF points from PyMuPDF). 23 of the user's 27 stored citations and 156 of 159 chunks have them, but the frontend never uses them. The user approved a ticket and a Sonnet agent.
